/P 137 0 R
/E (Privacy is understandable, but excessive privacy is impossible when entering the dating market. Dating is about searching for the right person to share your life, not hiding it. Until you are ready to be an open book, you should remain single. if you meet someone that is not ready to be open with you then it is best to end it right there or put it on pause until that person is ready to be open with you. we have couples that are roommates but call it a relationship. They know very little about each other. Finance is a secret, family is a secret, the relationship is a secret and that means a stranger is in your space.      )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
